  keywords = {AI Models, Automation, FutureTech, Innovation, JohnVonNeumann, Self Generative Systems, Technology},
  abstract = {This article begins by exploring the concept of self-reproducing automata, as introduced by John von Neumann [1]. According to the Wikipedia entry [8], the initial studies on self-reproducing automata date back to 1940. Over the span of more than 80 years, significant advancements have been made in this field of research and development, bringing us closer to the realization of systems capable of self-reproduction, which we will refer to as self-generative systems (SGS).}
}

