  publisher = {Association for Computing Machinery},
  address = {New York, NY, USA},
  doi = {10.1145/3786161},
  isbn = {9798400723933},
  abstract = {Welcome to the 7th International Workshop on Bots and Agents in Software Engineering (BoatSE), held in conjunction with the 48th ACM/IEEE International Conference on Software Engineering (ICSE 2026) in Rio de Janeiro, Brazil.BoatSE is the premier annual gathering for researchers and practitioners dedicated to the study and development of bots and agents in software engineering. This year marks a significant evolution in our community, reflected in our renamed title. While bots have become a reality in software engineering, automating tasks once performed by humans, the landscape is shifting. The latest developments in Generative Artificial Intelligence have brought forth a new type of software engineering tool: LLM-powered Agents. Agents hold the promise of automating more complex tasks and are an emerging research area that requires further collaboration to tackle new and open challenges. The goal of this one-day workshop is to bring together software engineering researchers and practitioners to discuss the latest state of the art and state of the practice of bots and agents in software engineering.}
}

